From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:09:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.system.profile: SharedModeSettings, and RetailInfo's
 factory as Windows has it.

Word asks for Windows.System.Profile.SharedModeSettings and found no
library for it.  Shared mode is a setting of devices many people use in
turn, under which applications are to keep nothing on the machine; this
is not such a device, so it is off and local storage is fine, as
Windows answers on every machine not set up that way.  Its factory is
Windows': statics only, neither agile nor marshaled, E_ILLEGAL_METHOD_CALL
for a class name, base trust, and the three interfaces in GetIids.

Measured next to it, RetailInfo's factory answered differently from
Windows' in three ways: its class name is E_ILLEGAL_METHOD_CALL rather
than E_NOTIMPL, its trust level is base trust, and it lists its
interfaces and marshals free-threaded.  Windows also lists a third,
internal interface nothing documents, which is left out here.

The tests pass on Windows as they do here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b21cb2a018d418c679c8ed092be659604b0e6171)

